{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "איש אל אחזתו", :translit "ish el achuzato", :gloss "each man to his holding"} {:he "וכי תמכרו ממכר לעמיתך", :translit "v'chi timkeru mimkar la'amitecha", :gloss "when you sell a sale to your fellow"} {:he "נכסים שאין להם אחריות", :translit "nechasim she'yeish lahem acharayut", :gloss "assets that have no guaranty"} {:he "נכסים שיש להם אחריות", :translit "nechasim she'yesh lahem acharayut", :gloss "assets that have guaranty"} {:he "אל תונו איש את עמיתו", :translit "al tonu ish et amito", :gloss "do not wrong one another"} {:he "איש לאחוזתו", :translit "ish la'achuzato", :gloss "each man to his holding"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (smikhut): adjacent verses teach legal inferences about acquisition and fraud."}], :frame {:text "The law of ona'ah (price fraud) applies to movable goods: a sale may be voided if overcharged by more than a sixth (Bava Metzi'a 49b–50b). Land, however, is generally exempt because the Torah's ona'ah verse speaks of selling 'to your fellow,' which was read as excluding land (Bava Metzi'a 56a). The question of whether movable property (which lacks guaranty) can be acquired through land (which has guaranty) via the mechanism of kinyan agav is discussed in Bava Batra 66a and related sugyot.", :sources ["Bava Metzi'a 49b" "Bava Metzi'a 50b" "Bava Metzi'a 56a" "Bava Batra 66a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (smikhut): adjacent verses teach legal inferences about acquisition and fraud.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:25:35.143043456Z", :model "glm-5.2"}